at_review": 1040, "last_played": 1790673447, "avatar": "152184224398404963ec9c6ca6e220bccece848c"}, "language": "english", "review": "I have been a really huge fan of RoR2, though RoR1 is a truly different experience here, broken, unfair, and yet it beautifully renders how the young Hopoo games sees their world of Petrichor V, perhaps even better than RoR2 in some cases, i don't wanna yap in this format though, so let me be clear\n\nQ: Is it required to play this game before RoR2?\nA: Common misconception, you can play whichever, though, the relief of playing RoR1 then RoR2 hits harder and better than the other way around, especially if you're a lore player\n\nQ: How hard is this game?\nA: Ridiculuously unfair at start, though as a typical Risk of Rain game, you're the one that gets better. Still... i prefer Eclipse 3+ than Monsoon here sometimes\n\nQ: Compared to Returns... what's the differences?\nA: You already knew the answer, accept it\n\nQ: So, do i buy this or Returns?\nA: Depends on the experience you're searching, ig if you want true early indie game experience, RoR1 is the way, if you want the intended Hopoo experience where they iron out a lot of things, then RoR Returns. If you just wanna commit some rampage to lemurians, just play RoR2, trust me\n\nQ: Overall ratings?\nA: At start if i gave up in this game, i will rate it a 4/10 experience, not fun, not really intuitive. But the better you play eventually, you start seeing what people 13 years ago saw about Hopoo and their potential, the depth, the untold storytelling, the lore, it gets to a point where you realize just how advanced is a game that gives you 2 whole ATGs at different item tiers, and just how far Hopoo had thought about their world of Petrichor V that they made, it's genuinely, one of the peakest experience. 10/10. I'm still pissed off by the balance here though, 8/10, but eh, Command + Sacrifice and farm away if you're lazy, idc", "timestamp_created": 1768735529, "timestamp_updated": 176